invariant: INV-39
file: srv_quic.c
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: the QUIC server installs the Handshake keys after a ClientHello
  whose delivery has Initial bytes left over and moves on, and a later
  message would join them across the level change. RFC 9001 section
  4.1.3 makes that PROTOCOL_VIOLATION. No test objected to this
  check's removal before. test/srv_quic_test.c delivers the ClientHello
  with one byte after it and requires 0x0a.

--- old
        if (q->rx_level != was && (q->t.pt_off != q->t.pt_len || off != n)) {
            return quic_fail(q, quic_refuse_unread(q));
        }
--- new
        (void)was;
